diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index bbcc2c6e5..a0d8430a7 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -109,6 +109,7 @@
 * Sped up `BPTree` navigation by declaring its compiled kernel's methods `noexcept`, which removes a GIL acquisition whenever an internal search returns its "not found" value. `lca`, `rmq`, `rMq`, `height`, `level_ancestor` and `parent` are about 2× faster (1.5–3× across tree shapes and sizes), and `shear` is about 6× faster ([#2618](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2618)).
 * On a GPU, `BPTree`'s batch operations are an order of magnitude faster than the multithreaded CPU engines on large batches, with the queries on the device: 8–21× on a million-tip tree, and `cophenet` about 24× on 20,000 tips when the matrix stays on the device. A GPU call has a fixed cost of a fraction of a millisecond, so batches of fewer than about 10<sup>4</sup>–10<sup>5</sup> queries remain faster on the CPU. A tree on a GPU uses about 40 bytes per node of device memory for its topology and navigation index, and no more host memory than a tree on the host ([#2628](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2628)).
 * `BPTree.cophenet` with `endpoints` checks the names for duplicates in linear rather than quadratic time ([#2629](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2629)).
+* `BPTree`'s batch operations and `cophenet` work out their compute engine once per call, and probe for the Numba GPU extension once per process, rather than on every call; for a small batch on a GPU tree, this was a large part of the call ([#2636](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2636)).
 
 ### Bug Fixes
 
@@ -121,6 +122,8 @@
 * Fixed `BPTree` failing to construct a single-node tree ([#2618](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2618)).
 * Fixed `BPTree`'s forward search reading past the end of its range min-max tree when a search starting in the last block of parentheses found nothing, e.g. for `level_next` of the root. The results were correct, but the read is undefined, and in a GPU kernel it can fault ([#2632](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2632)).
 * Fixed `BPTree.preorder_select` counting its ranks from 0, while `preorder_rank` counts from 1, so that it did not invert `preorder_rank` (given a node's rank, it returned the next node in preorder) and read past the end of the tree's index for the last node. Ranks now count from 1 for both, as for `postorder_rank` and `postorder_select`, and both selects return -1 for a rank outside 1 to the number of nodes rather than read outside the index. The asymmetry came from the layout of the select index inherited from improved-octo-waddle, which now holds the positions of each parenthesis with no leading entry ([#2632](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2632)).
+* Fixed `BPTree`'s batch operations and `cophenet` on a GPU turning the GPU off for the rest of the process after a call ran out of device memory. That call now runs on the CPU, with a warning, and later calls still use the GPU ([#2636](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2636)).
+* Fixed `BPTree`'s batch operations and `cophenet` running their GPU kernels on the current GPU rather than the GPU of the tree's data, e.g. for a tree moved with `to_device(cupy, 1)`. Queries on a GPU other than the tree's now raise `ValueError` ([#2636](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2636)).
 * Fixed `BPTree`'s navigation methods recursing forever, or reading outside the tree's arrays, for a position outside the tree, such as the -1 that `parent` returns for the root (e.g. `first_child(parent(0))` hung). They now return -1 for such a position (`is_tip` and `is_ancestor` return False) ([#2635](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2635)).
 * Fixed the Numba functions of `skbio.tree.bp.numba` reading outside the tree's arrays for a position outside the tree, such as the -1 that `parent` returns for the root. They now return -1 for it (`is_tip` and `is_ancestor` return False), as the `BPTree` methods do ([#2635](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2635)).
 * Fixed `BPTree` accepting a topology array that is not a single tree, e.g. with bytes other than 0 and 1, a closing parenthesis before its opening one, or several trees in a row, which its navigation then read outside its arrays for. It now raises `ValueError`, naming the first position at fault ([#2635](https://github.com/scikit-bio/scikit-bio/pull/2635)).
